From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini Mainline Experiment <gemini-mainline@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:17:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: aw8738: switch the amplifier on after the outputs that
 feed it

DAPM orders output drivers of the same type by register before component,
so the amplifier's widget, with no register, powers up before a codec
output driver that has one. On the Gemini PDA the AW8736 amplifiers were
on 90 ms before the MT6351 headphone outputs that feed them started their
power-up, and their transient was heard on the speakers.

Give the amplifier a later DAPM sub-sequence. It then powers up after the
other output drivers and down before them, as amplifiers should.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/aw8738.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/aw8738.c b/sound/soc/codecs/aw8738.c
index aa0a48e..fb4bd42 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/aw8738.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/aw8738.c
@@ -41,8 +41,15 @@ static int aw8738_drv_event(struct snd_soc_dapm_widget *w,
 
 static const struct snd_soc_dapm_widget aw8738_dapm_widgets[] = {
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_INPUT("IN"),
-	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUT_DRV_E("DRV", SND_SOC_NOPM, 0, 0, NULL, 0, aw8738_drv_event,
-			       SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMD),
+	{
+		.id = snd_soc_dapm_out_drv,
+		.name = "DRV",
+		.reg = SND_SOC_NOPM,
+		.event = aw8738_drv_event,
+		.event_flags = SND_SOC_DAPM_POST_PMU | SND_SOC_DAPM_PRE_PMD,
+		/* After the outputs that feed it on power-up, before them on power-down */
+		.subseq = 1,
+	},
 	SND_SOC_DAPM_OUTPUT("OUT"),
 };
 
